  "summary": "I wrote `src/main.ts`, and it passes `typecheck`. I couldn't run the build or view a frame (no shell or browser), so the look and the particle behaviour are untested.\n\n- **Crystals:** There are seven, each built with `geometry.define` and `geometry.custom`. Each is a 5- or 6-sided prism with a pointed top, drawn as non-indexed triangles with one normal per face, so the shading is flat. Every face has its own colour. Heights run from 1.2 to 3.1 and the tilts are all different.\n- **Rotation:** The crystals sit in a group that spins slowly (0.35 rad/s) on a dark cylindrical pedestal.\n- **Sparks:** An `effects.particles` emitter with additive blending, a negative gravity value (so the sparks should drift upward) and a little noise. The scene also has bloom. The emitter's direction and the sign of the gravity value are my reading of the docs, so check that the sparks rise rather than fall.\n- **Look:** The background is near-black. A dim warm key light comes from the front. Cyan and magenta directional lights from behind act as rim lights.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after `app.ready()`, once the next `requestAnimationFrame` callback runs. Frames change over time because of the spin and the particles.\n\n",
